    "body": "This (and all others) need to do an explicit alignment check (read_memory will only do it based on the MISALIGNED_LDST parameter).\n\nYou probably need a new function in globals.isa that looks a lot like the `amo` function, but does a normal read or write instead of an amo.\n\nFor operations with release, there is also the complication that the release shouldn't occur if the load/store is going to cause an exception. I'll let you think about how to convey that, but it's probably going to require some handling the new function.",
